{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Origin","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Extracts "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scheme:\/\/host[:port]"},{"type":"text","text":" from any URL. Path, query, and fragment are stripped."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Enforces the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/w3c.github.io\/webappsec-secure-contexts\/"},{"type":"text","text":":"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/"},{"type":"text","text":" is accepted, with an exception for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/localhost"},{"type":"text","text":" (and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*.localhost"},{"type":"text","text":") for local development. The origin concept itself is defined by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tools.ietf.org\/html\/rfc6454"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let origin = try WebAuthn.Origin(\"https:\/\/example.com\/login?foo=bar\")","\/\/ origin.stringValue == \"https:\/\/example.com\"","","let withPort = try WebAuthn.Origin(\"https:\/\/example.com:8443\/api\")","\/\/ withPort.stringValue == \"https:\/\/example.com:8443\"","","let localhost = try WebAuthn.Origin(\"http:\/\/localhost:3000\")  \/\/ allowed for development","","let insecure = try WebAuthn.Origin(\"http:\/\/example.com\")  \/\/ throws .insecureContext"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A validated WebAuthn origin ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scheme:\/\/host[:port]"},{"type":"text","tex